{{Quote|That's the problem with a sniper rifle. Deadly at a distance&hellip;but vulnerable at close range.|[[Gallin Crae]], to [[Just Lucky]]|<ref name="Doctor Aphra (2020) 12">[[Doctor Aphra (2020) 12|''Doctor Aphra'' (2020) 12]]</ref>}}
The '''sniper rifle''', also called a '''sniper blaster rifle''' or '''assassin rifle''', was a type of [[blaster rifle]] used to shoot targets at long range. Though some rifles were built as sniper rifles, many other models could be used as one with the addition of a [[scope]] and other accessories like a [[stock]].

==History==
[[File:Sniper_Rifle_The_Box.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Obi-Wan Kenobi disguised as Rako Hardeen fires a sniper rifle in the Box.]]
Just before the [[Clone Wars]], [[Zam Wesell]] used a flying [[assassin droid]] in an [[Plot to assassinate Senator Amidala|attempt to assassinate]] [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] on [[Coruscant]]. The plan failed, and Zam Wesell saw the assassin droid returning to her with [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] hanging onto it. To avoid being caught by the [[Jedi]] and having her plans exposed, Wesell retrieved her sniper rifle from her [[airspeeder]]. Using the targeting [[scope]] on her [[KiSteer 1284 projectile rifle]] to zoom in on her target, she fired at the incoming droid and destroyed it. This sent Kenobi plummeting toward the planet surface, but he was quickly rescued by [[Anakin Skywalker]]. Realizing things had gone south, Wesell immediately stowed her sniper rifle and took off in her airspeeder.<ref name="Episode II: Attack of the Clones" />

During the Clone Wars, a [[BX-series droid commando]] used a sniper rifle at the [[Battle of Saleucami]] to wound [[Rex]].<ref name="TD">{{TCW|The Deserter}}</ref> [[Bounty hunter]]s such as [[Aurra Sing]],<ref name="Assassin">{{TCW|Assassin (episode)}}</ref> [[Rumi Paramita]],<ref name="Bounty Hunters">{{TCW|Bounty Hunters (episode)}}</ref> and [[Rako Hardeen]]<ref name="Deception">{{TCW|Deception}}</ref> used these rifles in their jobs. A [[Unidentified Death Watch assassin|Death Watch assassin]] used a sniper rifle in a failed attempt to assassinate [[Satine Kryze]] on [[Coruscant]]. [[Onderon rebels]]' leader [[Steela Gerrera]] used one in her fight to [[Onderonian Civil War|liberate]] [[Onderon]].<ref name="A War on Two Fronts">{{TCW|A War on Two Fronts}}</ref> 

[[File:DLT-19xSniper-SWL.png|thumb|right|250px|A scout trooper using a DLT-19x targeting blaster]]
The defective clone [[Crosshair]] used a [[773 Firepuncher sniper rifle|773 Firepuncher rifle]] during the Clone Wars and continued to use the weapon to deadly effect in service to the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Devil's Deal">{{TBB|Devil's Deal}}</ref> During the [[Assault on Cymoon]], Chewbacca used a sniper rifle to attack Darth Vader, who deflected all of his shots before using [[the Force]] to topple the building Chewbacca was perched upon.<ref name="SW12">[[Star Wars (2015) 1|''Star Wars'' (2015) 1]]</ref> [[Han Solo]] used a [[DLT-20A blaster rifle]] as a sniper rifle during the [[Battle of Vrogas Vas]].<ref name="SW 13">[[Star Wars (2015) 13|''Star Wars'' (2015) 13]]</ref>

In the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Stormtrooper Corps]], [[stormtrooper sniper]]s were equipped with sniper rifles<ref name="Recon Missions">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Recon Missions]]''</ref> including the [[DLT-19x targeting blaster]].<ref name="Legion">{{Legion|set=Scout Troopers Unit Expansion|cardname=DLT-19x Sniper}}</ref> Agent [[Del Meeko]] of the [[Inferno Squad]] used a sniper rifle during the [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="Battlefront">''[[Star Wars Battlefront]]''</ref> 

In the [[New Republic Era|New Republic era]], [[Fennec Shand]] used an [[785MK Firepuncher-X sniper rifle|MK sniper rifle]] to snipe bounty hunters [[Din Djarin]] and [[Toro Calican]].<ref name="Chapter 5">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 5: The Gunslinger}}</ref> [[Migs Mayfeld]] used a [[cycler rifle]] with great accuracy to destroy [[rhydonium]] shipments on [[Morak]] while standing aboard a boarding ramp of [[Boba Fett]]'s ''[[Slave I]]''.<ref name="Chapter 15">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 15: The Believer}}</ref>

